From 5af111fea4c9a2ecda49137d2866b6196939ff21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kazhiramatsu <kazutakehiramatsu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:38:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] draft(A6-41 item 4, follow-up): emitted computed names are
 never re-entered

The memo audit fired on outer-this-computed-name: a decorated static
property's rewritten computed name carries pending expressions that were
visited under earlier members' frames (a method decorator keeps lexical
this), and the property update re-visited that name under the static
element frame; the node-id memo happened to return the earlier result, but
tsc's updateComputedPropertyName never re-enters the name. The emitted name
is now memoized as visited, so no already-projected subtree is re-entered
under another receiver context (a synthesized this receiver of a super
decorator would otherwise be rewritten).
---
 crates/emitter/src/builtins/standard_decorators.rs | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/emitter/src/builtins/standard_decorators.rs b/crates/emitter/src/builtins/standard_decorators.rs
index afdc2fcf8..75a58353f 100644
--- a/crates/emitter/src/builtins/standard_decorators.rs
+++ b/crates/emitter/src/builtins/standard_decorators.rs
@@ -2442,6 +2442,10 @@ impl<'context> StandardDecoratorVisitor<'context> {
             }
             _ => self.create_computed_property_name(injected)?,
         };
+        // The emitted name holds already-visited pending expressions (visited
+        // under their own members' frames); tsc never re-enters it, so the
+        // member update must not visit it again under this element's frame.
+        self.nodes.insert(name.node(), Some(name.node()));
         Ok((temporary_binding, name))
     }
 
